  "body": "## Finding description and impact\n\n\nThe `MEVCapture` extension charges an additional fee when swaps cross tick spacings, calculated as `additionalFee = ticksCrossed * poolFee`. This fee is designed to capture MEV from large swaps that significantly move the price. However, the fee calculation logic differs between ExactIn and ExactOut swaps. For ExactOut swaps, the code first removes the base pool fee from the input amount, and then calculates the additional fee on the reduced amount. This means the additional fee is computed on a smaller base. For ExactIn swaps, the code calculates the additional fee directly on the full output amount without any prior deduction of the pool fee. This inconsistency results in ExactIn users paying a higher effective fee than ExactOut users for equivalent trades. The difference becomes more pronounced as more tick spacings are crossed and the additional fee grows larger. The PoC demonstrates this with two identical pools using 1% pool fee and tickSpacing of 10. An ExactIn swap paying 100,000 tokens receives a certain output. An ExactOut swap requesting that same output only costs 95,209 tokens - a difference of 4,790 tokens (4.79%).\n\n### Impact\n- ExactIn users are overcharged compared to ExactOut users for identical effective trades\n- The discrepancy scales with tick spacings crossed\n- Sophisticated traders gain an advantage by always using ExactOut swaps\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nUse consistent fee calculation logic for both swap directions to ensure users pay the same amount regardless of whether they specify exact input or exact output.",
  "proof_of_concept": "```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: ekubo-license-v1.eth\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport {console} from \"forge-std/console.sol\";\nimport {createSwapParameters} from \"../../src/types/swapParameters.sol\";\nimport {PoolKey} from \"../../src/types/poolKey.sol\";\nimport {createConcentratedPoolConfig} from \"../../src/types/poolConfig.sol\";\nimport {SqrtRatio} from \"../../src/types/sqrtRatio.sol\";\nimport {FullTest} from \"../FullTest.sol\";\nimport {MEVCapture, mevCaptureCallPoints} from \"../../src/extensions/MEVCapture.sol\";\nimport {MEVCaptureRouter} from \"../../src/MEVCaptureRouter.sol\";\nimport {PoolBalanceUpdate} from \"../../src/types/poolBalanceUpdate.sol\";\nimport {CoreLib} from \"../../src/libraries/CoreLib.sol\";\nimport {TestToken} from \"../TestToken.sol\";\n\n/**\n * @title MEVCapture Fee Asymmetry PoC\n * @notice Demonstrates fee asymmetry between exactIn and exactOut swaps\n *\n * Setup: Two identical pools\n * Pool1: ExactIn swap - pay X token0, receive Y token1\n * Pool2: ExactOut swap - request Y token1, pay Z token0\n *\n * Expected: X == Z (same cost for same output)\n * Actual: X != Z due to different fee calculations\n */\ncontract MEVCaptureFeeAsymmetryTest is FullTest {\n    using CoreLib for *;\n\n    MEVCapture internal mevCapture;\n\n    TestToken internal tokenA;\n    TestToken internal tokenB;\n\n    function setUp() public override {\n        FullTest.setUp();\n        address deployAddress = address(uint160(mevCaptureCallPoints().toUint8()) << 152);\n        deployCodeTo(\"MEVCapture.sol\", abi.encode(core), deployAddress);\n        mevCapture = MEVCapture(deployAddress);\n        router = new MEVCaptureRouter(core, address(mevCapture));\n\n        // Create second pair of tokens for Pool2\n        TestToken tA = new TestToken(address(this));\n        TestToken tB = new TestToken(address(this));\n        (tokenA, tokenB) = address(tA) < address(tB) ? (tA, tB) : (tB, tA);\n    }\n\n    /**\n     * @notice PoC: Two identical pools, compare exactIn vs exactOut costs\n     */\n    function test_poc_fee_asymmetry() public {\n        uint64 poolFee = uint64((uint256(1) << 64) / 100); // 1%\n        uint32 tickSpacing = 10;\n        uint128 liqAmount = 1000000e18;  // 500K liquidity, swap is 20%\n\n        // Wider range to allow crossing more tick spacings\n        int32 tickLower = -2000;\n        int32 tickUpper = 2000;\n\n        // === Create Pool 1 (for exactIn) ===\n        PoolKey memory pool1 = createPool(\n            address(token0),\n            address(token1),\n            0,\n            createConcentratedPoolConfig(poolFee, tickSpacing, address(mevCapture))\n        );\n        createPosition(pool1, tickLower, tickUpper, liqAmount, liqAmount);\n\n        // === Create Pool 2 (for exactOut) - identical setup ===\n        PoolKey memory pool2 = createPool(\n            address(tokenA),\n            address(tokenB),\n            0,\n            createConcentratedPoolConfig(poolFee, tickSpacing, address(mevCapture))\n        );\n        tokenA.approve(address(positions), liqAmount);\n        tokenB.approve(address(positions), liqAmount);\n        positions.mintAndDeposit(pool2, tickLower, tickUpper, liqAmount, liqAmount, 0);\n\n        // Approve tokens for swaps\n        token0.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        token1.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        tokenA.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n        tokenB.approve(address(router), type(uint256).max);\n\n        // === Pool 1: ExactIn swap ===\n        // Smaller amount to cross only ~2-3 tick spacings\n        int128 inputAmount = 100_000e18;\n\n        PoolBalanceUpdate result1 = router.swap({\n            poolKey: pool1,\n            params: createSwapParameters({\n                _isToken1: false,\n                _amount: inputAmount,  // positive = exactIn\n                _sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0),\n                _skipAhead: 0\n            }),\n            calculatedAmountThreshold: type(int256).min,\n            recipient: address(this)\n        });\n\n        int128 exactIn_paid = result1.delta0();      // positive = user pays\n        int128 exactIn_received = -result1.delta1(); // negative flipped = user receives\n\n        console.log(\"=== Pool 1: ExactIn ===\");\n        console.log(\"Input (token0 paid):\", uint256(int256(exactIn_paid)));\n        console.log(\"Output (token1 received):\", uint256(int256(exactIn_received)));\n\n        // === Pool 2: ExactOut for SAME output ===\n        PoolBalanceUpdate result2 = router.swap({\n            poolKey: pool2,\n            params: createSwapParameters({\n                _isToken1: true,\n                _amount: -exactIn_received,  // negative = exactOut this amount\n                _sqrtRatioLimit: SqrtRatio.wrap(0),\n                _skipAhead: 0\n            }),\n            calculatedAmountThreshold: type(int256).min,\n            recipient: address(this)\n        });\n\n        int128 exactOut_paid = result2.delta0();      // positive = user pays\n        int128 exactOut_received = -result2.delta1(); // negative flipped = user receives\n\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"=== Pool 2: ExactOut (same output target) ===\");\n        console.log(\"Input (tokenA paid):\", uint256(int256(exactOut_paid)));\n        console.log(\"Output (tokenB received):\", uint256(int256(exactOut_received)));\n\n        // === Compare ===\n        console.log(\"\");\n        console.log(\"=== Comparison ===\");\n\n        uint256 inCost = uint256(int256(exactIn_paid));\n        uint256 outCost = uint256(int256(exactOut_paid));\n\n        console.log(\"Same output received:\", uint256(int256(exactIn_received)) == uint256(int256(exactOut_received)));\n        console.log(\"ExactIn cost:\", inCost);\n        console.log(\"ExactOut cost:\", outCost);\n\n        if (inCost > outCost) {\n            console.log(\"RESULT: ExactIn pays MORE by\", inCost - outCost);\n        } else if (outCost > inCost) {\n            console.log(\"RESULT: ExactOut pays MORE by\", outCost - inCost);\n        } else {\n            console.log(\"RESULT: Equal (no asymmetry)\");\n        }\n\n        // The vulnerability: costs should be equal but aren't\n        assertTrue(inCost != outCost, \"Fee asymmetry exists\");\n    }\n}\n\n```",
